ticularly the testicles actually  this can drastically increase  testosterone and this works in a  different way  from just raising vitamin d it actually  boosts and encourages  mitochondrial performance these being  the energy factories of the cell  or the powerhouses of the cell as  everyone likes to say and this also  affects the leydig cells  which in turn results in a massively  elevated testosterone boost  other research looking at red light  therapy is also really positive it can  encourage blood flow which at the same  time can  improve healing and it generally  stimulates energy production so  this is something that i could imagine  batman doing in his home having a big  wall of red light it's not something  i've personally experimented with yet  i would like to but in the meantime just  getting more sunlight  you know training outdoors and taking  your top off from time to time can be  really good  this is actually something i think makes  intuitive sense many of the people that  i've known  in my own life who have the most energy  and seem the healthiest  are the outdoorsy types people who are  surfers or like riding mountain bikes or  hiking these people just seem to have  boundless energy  and there might be a good reason for  that you see there is a reason for all  of the gratuitous nudity on this channel  so that's it for part one guys this  video was getting so long i decided i'd  split it into two parts here we talked  about sleep and recovery  and next time i'm going to be talking  about diet supplements and bio hacks  that  bruce wayne or someone who trains  intensely might use in order to  help themselves push themselves further  hope you found this useful and  interesting if you did guys then please  leave a like and share around  that helps me out immensely likewise  leave any comments below  let me know what different strategies  you use to get the most out of your  sleep especially  when you don't have enough time to sleep  properly if you like the idea of  training  and biohacking not only for strength but  for cognitive performance and for better  sleep and  agility and flexibility and endurance  then you might enjoy my ebook and  training program super functional  training  you'll find that in the description down  below and there's a discount on right  now whilst we're dealing with a pandemic  likewise like i said you can also find a  link to the muse 2 headband if you're  interested in that  i also have a print book out it's called  functional training and beyond and there  i discuss  functional training and what it means  for the general population as well as  athletes so  that serves as a great introduction i  hope either way thank you so much for  watching for supporting the channel for  subscribing it really means a lot to me  and i'll catch you next time  bye for now
 

